        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-01-09T03:10:53.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"McBehrer\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mcbehrer/48/1850_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> McBehrer:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>That being said, I don't believe Potent Disruption requires the actual destruction, so you could use it, deal damage, and play a card off of it, I think.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I agree with this, tenatively. &nbsp;The one problem I see is the way it is worded, while not including a \"if you do\" has you deal damage equal to the hp of the destroyed card, if the card was not destroyed, does it still deal damage? &nbsp;If so would it work through Fixed Point?</p>",
